  "compiled_truth": "No, ChatGPT does not \"Scare Google\" - by Michael Spencer\n            \n            \n            \n            \n        \n\n        \n\n        \n\n        \n        \n        \n        \n        \n        \n        \n        \n        \n\n        \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n                \n            \n        \n\n        \n        \n        \n        \n        \n        \n        \n        \n        \n        \n        \n\n        \n\n        \n            \n        \n\n        \n\n        \n            \n                \n            \n        \n            \n                \n            \n        \n            \n                \n            \n        \n            \n                \n            \n        \n            \n                \n            \n        \n            \n                \n            \n        \n            \n                \n            \n        \n            \n                \n            \n        \n            \n                \n            \n        \n            \n                \n            \n        \n            \n                \n            \n        \n            \n                \n            \n        \n            \n                \n            \n        \n            \n                \n            \n        \n            \n                \n            \n        \n            \n        \n            \n        \n            \n        \n\n        \n\n        \n            \n        \n\n        \n        \n          \n        \n        \n        \n\n        \n\n        \n            \n        \n            \n        \n\n        \n\n        \n\n        \n\n        \n\n        \n            \n        \n    \n\n    \n        \n\n        \n            \n        \n\n        \n\n        \n\n        \n            AI Supremacy \n\nSubscribeSign inFlash No, ChatGPT does not \"Scare Google\"\n\nWhat is Neeva Search? Reality: Google has 91.88% of search market. \n\nMichael SpencerDec 08, 2022∙ Paid5Share\n\nHey Everyone, \n\nI too am recovering from the ChatGPT hype bomb that OpenAI’s limited demo has created. There’s a lot of misinformation I’m seeing and one of the worst things is perhaps how ‘ChatGPT will threaten the future of search’. \n\nWhile this may be true one day when Conversational AI is vastly improved, even Google cannot get this right, we are at least a decade from that period in 2022. \n\nA good search engine is about real-time data and fact verification, among other things like freedom from Ads. If Microsoft internalizes chatGPT into Bing, I am not bullish the demo suffered too many A.I. alignment issues. \n\nThat does stop the idea that ChatGPT could disrupt search or Google, from going viral: \n\njosh@jdjkellyGoogle is done.\n\nCompare the quality of these responses (ChatGPT) 6:29 PM · Nov 30, 20223.76K Reposts · 24.7K LikesGoogle is essentially more advanced than OpenAI at its own game, it has LaMDA 2 among other things. ChatGPT is a fun demo, it is not a new paradigm. I think this was fairly expressed and hijacked by a Search startup Neeva recently. \n\nNeeva’s founder seeing an opportunity and integrating LLMs anyways tweeted the following: \n\n<span class=\\\"tweet-fake-link\\\">@Neeva</span></span>, we've been revolutionizing search w/ an ad free, privacy-first model\\n\\nBut we’ve also been quietly upgrading the experience entirely w/cutting edge AI &amp; LLMs.\\n\\nChatGPT cannot give you real time data or fact verification. In our upcoming upgrades, <span class=\\\"tweet-fake-link\\\"><span class=\\\"tweet-fake-link\\\">@Neeva</span></span> can \",\"username\":\"RamaswmySridhar\",\"name\":\"ramaswamy.eth\",\"profile_image_url\":\"\",\"date\":\"Tue Dec 06 19:23:03 +0000 2022\",\"photos\":[{\"img_url\":\"https://pbs.substack.com/media/FjUVZMjVQAEVs3i.jpg\",\"link_url\":\"https://t.co/H44EUacLcC\",\"alt_text\":null}],\"quoted_tweet\":{},\"reply_count\":0,\"retweet_count\":94,\"like_count\":785,\"impression_count\":0,\"expanded_url\":{},\"video_url\":null,\"belowTheFold\":true}\" class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-flexDirection-column pc-gap-12 pc-padding-16 pc-reset bg-primary-zk6FDl outline-detail-vcQLyr pc-borderRadius-md sizing-border-box-DggLA4 pressable-lg-kV7yq8 font-text-qe4AeH tweet-fWkQfo twitter-embed\">ramaswamy.eth@RamaswmySridharAt @Neeva, we've been revolutionizing search w/ an ad free, privacy-first model\n\nBut we’ve also been quietly upgrading the experience entirely w/cutting edge AI & LLMs.\n\nChatGPT cannot give you real time data or fact verification. In our upcoming upgrades, @Neeva can 7:23 PM · Dec 6, 202294 Reposts · 785 LikesNeeva is trying to be for honest results. \n\nDownload today: \n\n Google Play - https://bit.ly/3PzAUFT \n\n App Store - https://apple.co/35IalJ5\n\nThis isn’t a sponsored Ad, but you can download the chrome extension also here I noticed. \n\nShare\n\nContinue reading this post for free, courtesy of Michael Spencer.\n\nClaim my free postOr purchase a paid subscription.PreviousNext© 2026 Michael Spencer · Privacy ∙ Terms ∙ Collection notice Start your SubstackGet the appSubstack is the home for great culture\n        \n\n        \n            \n            \n        \n\n        \n        \n        \n        \n        \n        \n        \n\n        \n        \n            \n                \n            